kind how-do-i
title How do I give a look a vtlook on the command line?
intro `vtium-config look set` sets each setting of a look, and `--vtlook` names the look's vtlook, the file of filters such as an amber tint. It sets the same line as the vtlook line of a look's card.
see effects/give-a-look-a-vtlook

file etc/vtium.conf
    version = 1
    font-name = unifont
    [look plain]
    palette = legacy
    [head console]
    vt = 5
    look = plain
file etc/batch.conf
    ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
font fonts/mono.bdf 8x16
frit mono
    source=bdf:ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
file etc/looks/amber.vtlook
    version = 1
    [color tint]
    color = 255,176,0
    amount = 1.0
    floor = 0.0

1. Press q to quit.
2. Run `vtium-config look set plain --vtlook amber`.
at the vtlook is set
check draft look plain vtlook amber
3. Run `vtium-config install`.
at the install
check installed look plain vtlook amber
